bcg.bedrock_core.commands.nav=Commands
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.intro=Every addon built on bedrock-core shares this screen. The list on the left is every addon installed in this world; pick one to reach its settings or its own guide.
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.title=Commands
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.namespace=Each addon registers its own commands under its own namespace, written as creator_pack. An addon by "bt" called "gc_graves" answers to bt_gc_graves. Type a slash and the start of a namespace to see what it offers.
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.cmd_config=§econfig§r - open that addon's settings: the scope picker if you are an operator, your own settings otherwise
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.cmd_get=§econfig get <setting>§r - read one of your own settings
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.cmd_set=§econfig set <setting> <value>§r - change one of your own settings
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.cmd_guide=§eguide§r - open that addon's guide, a page like this one
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.cmd_list=§elist§r - open the addon list, the screen behind this one
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.autocomplete=Settings autocomplete: the chat box offers the ones that addon actually has.
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.h2=Operators
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.operators=Anyone can read and change their own settings. Changing what applies to the whole server, to a dimension, or to another player needs operator, and those commands are hidden from everyone else.
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.cmd_getat=§econfigat get <scope.setting> [target]§r
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.cmd_setat=§econfigat set <scope.setting> <value> [target]§r
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.scoped=The scope is part of the setting - server.pricing.tax_rate, player.allow_gifts. For a dimension or player setting, [target] names which one; leave it out to mean yourself, or the dimension you are standing in.
bcg.bedrock_core.commands.tip=Command blocks can run configat, so server settings can be driven by redstone or a datapack-style setup.
